I have a shiny app that used to run on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> server (was uploaded in February).   App still runs locally.    However, on deployment to shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> server, the app now fails (see below) :  oauth_listener() needs an interactive environment

googlesheets author jennybc suggested a fix, getting a new .httr-oauth file in my working directory, https://github.com/jennybc/googlesheets/issues/235    This fix did not work.   I tried replacing the newest version of googlesheets package (0.2.0) on CRAN with an earlier version 0.1.0.9001, in case the updated googlesheets package had indeed caused the problem.   Same error with the earlier version.

It looks like my app on the shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> server is trying to communicate/authorize with Google Drive in interactive mode,.   Looking for suggestions to repair, as this is a production app for my team and now we're dead in the water.  Thank you!

